.TH TLS12PRFTEST 1
.SH NAME
tls12prftest \- test tls12->prf()
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tls12prftest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tls12prftest
checks
.BR prf() ,
TLS 1.2's own PRF construction (RFC 5246 \(sc5;
.IR module/tls12.m ,
.IR appl/lib/crypt/tls12.b ),
against four vectors. RFC 5246 gives the algorithm itself but no
worked examples, so these were generated from a from-scratch Python
reimplementation of that exact construction (real
.B hmac
/
.B hashlib
calls, not fabricated output, not recalled from memory) \(em the same
independent-oracle approach
.IR hmacsha256test (1)
used for the primitive this is built on.
.PP
Cases cover a short single-HMAC-block output, a 48-byte output (the
length TLS's own \(lqmaster secret\(rq derivation uses, forcing two
blocks), a 100-byte output (forcing four, so the block-boundary and
final-block truncation logic is exercised), and the degenerate
empty-secret case.
.PP
This is primitive 2 of the SSL modernization plan (see
.IR doc/ssl-modernization-plan.md
in the source tree), built directly on
.BR hmac_sha256() ,
primitive 1.
.PP
Exits with
.B PASS
if every vector matched, or
.B FAIL
naming which case, the expected bytes, and the bytes actually
produced.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/tls12prftest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR hmacsha256test (1)
.SH BUGS
Four vectors from one independent reimplementation, not cross-checked
against a second, unrelated TLS library's own intermediate PRF output
(no such published vectors were found for TLS 1.2's PRF specifically,
unlike HMAC-SHA256 itself, which RFC 4231 already publishes).
